From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marcel Ritter <marcel@linux-ng.de>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [core,nego] answer an unsupported Remote Credential Guard
 request

When a client requires Remote Credential Guard
(REDIRECTED_AUTHENTICATION_MODE_REQUIRED in the RDP_NEG_REQ, e.g.
"mstsc /remoteGuard" or the Windows policy "Restrict delegation of
credentials to remote servers: Require Remote Credential Guard") and the
server does not support it, nego_process_negotiation_request() failed
and the server closed the TCP connection without any X.224 Connection
Confirm. The client could only report a generic network error.

[MS-RDPBCGR] 2.2.1.2.1 lets the server say whether it supports the mode:
REDIRECTED_AUTHENTICATION_MODE_SUPPORTED in the RDP_NEG_RSP. None of the
RDP_NEG_FAILURE codes (2.2.1.2.2) describes the case. Continue instead,
so that the server sends an RDP_NEG_RSP without the flag. A client that
requires the mode then disconnects on its own and can say why (the
FreeRDP client logs "remote credential guard requested but not
supported"). The server-side Remote Credential Guard state stays off.

The case where the client also sets RESTRICTED_ADMIN_MODE_REQUIRED
("either mode") is unchanged.
---
 libfreerdp/core/nego.c | 13 +++++++++----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libfreerdp/core/nego.c b/libfreerdp/core/nego.c
index 723784e..621a38d 100644
--- a/libfreerdp/core/nego.c
+++ b/libfreerdp/core/nego.c
@@ -1352,10 +1352,15 @@ BOOL nego_process_negotiation_request(rdpNego* nego, wStream* s)
 			}
 			else
 			{
-				WLog_Print(
-				    nego->log, WLOG_ERROR,
-				    "RDP_NEG_REQ::flags REDIRECTED_AUTHENTICATION_MODE_REQUIRED but disabled");
-				return FALSE;
+				/* [MS-RDPBCGR] 2.2.1.2.1: the server states Remote Credential Guard support
+				 * with REDIRECTED_AUTHENTICATION_MODE_SUPPORTED in its RDP_NEG_RSP. Answer
+				 * without that flag (nego_send_negotiation_response) instead of dropping the
+				 * TCP connection, so that the client can tell its user why it cannot
+				 * connect; no RDP_NEG_FAILURE code (2.2.1.2.2) describes this case. A client
+				 * that requires the mode disconnects. RemoteCredsGuardActive stays FALSE. */
+				WLog_Print(nego->log, WLOG_WARN,
+				           "RDP_NEG_REQ::flags REDIRECTED_AUTHENTICATION_MODE_REQUIRED but "
+				           "disabled, answering without REDIRECTED_AUTHENTICATION_MODE_SUPPORTED");
 			}
 		}
 	}
